{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Raw project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/PLAN.md'","aggregated_output":"# Manufacturing implementation execution\n\nReadiness updated 2026-10-06: implementation is present and saved; overall G0–G6 acceptance remains open. Resume from the [recovered implementation handoff](continuation-handoff-2026-10-06.md), the current table below and latest leaf evidence. The accepted plan and owner storyline remain authoritative; unsupported tooling claims cannot pass on concept approval alone.\n\n## Contract\n\n- Preserve Default.glb, approved CAD sources, narrative ladder and station/opening windows. No staging, commit, push or deployment in this task.\n- Hash and measure in the shaft-local datum, with exactly one mm-to-m conversion and measured export registration. Approved supports already contain their final shift.\n- Producers edit only their assigned paths. No worker may revert another session's edits.\n- G0 assets: scripts/manufacturing/* measurement/export helpers and this evidence folder's geometry/ subtree, plus gates/assets.md.\n- G0 camera: this evidence folder's camera/ subtree and gates/camera.md. Read accepted source and measurements; propose compatible illustrative tool envelopes with explicit unresolved status when necessary.\n- G0 lifecycle: this evidence folder's lifecycle-contract.md and gates/lifecycle-contract.md. Read current lifecycle/camera/rig source; define adapter and restore contracts without modifying shared source.\n- Ring sampler refinement: src/scene/inspection/timeline.ts, timeline.test.ts, ringGeometry.ts and ringGeometry.test.ts; evidence ring/ and gates/ring-sampler.md. Shared scene/camera remain integration-owned. Independent sampler work may proceed from the fresh ring baseline while shaft G0 runs.\n- Core asset preparation: scripts/manufacturing/export_study.py, public/models/manufacturing-core-full.glb and manufacturing-core-lite.glb; evidence assets/ and gates/core-assets.md. Geometry reduction is preparation only; tooling/progression and G2 acceptance wait for reviewed G0.\n- G1 integration (Leibniz): CameraRig.tsx, TorqueWrenchHero.tsx, InspectionScene.tsx, SceneCanvas.tsx, PostProcessingComposer.tsx; new renderLease.ts/tests and ringRuntime.ts; narrativeFade.ts only as required. Runtime factory root and readiness are explicit typed interfaces. No shaft placeholder scene or missing-asset entry is permitted.\n- Parent owns root GATES.md, this PLAN.md, baseline evidence, review ledger and integration assignments.\n- Runtime verifier owns scripts/verify-manufacturing-inspection.mjs and evidence runtime/ only; it reports shared-source defects to the integration/shell owners and never patches them.\n- Shared integration edits in CameraRig.tsx, TorqueWrenchHero.tsx and InspectionScene.tsx belong to exactly one integration owner at a time. Earlier named assignments below are historical; establish current ownership before resuming edits.\n- Implemented interface baseline: kind ring|shaft; descriptors own duration, chapters and assets; one mutable absolute playhead; CameraRig sole camera writer; versioned manufacturing telemetry with backward-compatible ring telemetry; inspection-local assembled finale; instance-owned cloned resources with stale-session leases. Runtime acceptance remains separate from interface implementation.\n- Every stage has fresh review from a different provider and independently rerun checks. Requested model and observed routing evidence are recorded separately; flags alone are not served-model proof.\n\n## Tree And State\n\nReconciled 2026-10-06 against the final status log, leaf reports, runtime JSON and recovered source. Producer/reviewer completion does not close the overall gates. No listed worker should be assumed to be running from an older assignment.\n\n| Leaf | State | Needs | Gates |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| G0-assets | MEASURED; A1–A4 checked | final mechanical acceptance and gate reconciliation | gates/assets.md; geometry/; mechanical-review/ |\n| G0-camera / clearance | v4 CERTIFIED 24/24; earlier v3 invalid and superseded | residual mechanical review, C2 camera blockout and C4 budgets/commands | gates/camera.md; camera/clearance-v4/ |\n| G0-contract | VERIFIED INTERFACE | parent cross-provider contract-review.md | gates/lifecycle-contract.md |\n| G0-integration-review | OPEN | remaining G0-camera evidence and independent acceptance | root G0 |\n| G1-shell | GLM SHIP and parent rerun recorded; render-light restore fixed | fresh integration-wide acceptance | gates/shell.md |\n| G1-integration | IMPLEMENTED: ring and shaft registered, static/UI layers mounted, finale rig lookup corrected | reconcile I1–I5 with fresh production proof | gates/integration.md |\n| G1-runtime-verification | EXECUTED: lifecycle 12/14 twice; verifier GLM SHIP | V4 reduced-motion narrative CAD-loading decision/fix; V6 parent rerun | gates/runtime.md; runtime/lifecycle/ |\n| G2-core assets | EXPORTED: full/lite, eight nodes including approved/legacy housing witnesses | D4 independent export acceptance; overall G2 evidence | gates/core-assets.md; assets/core-assets-report-v3.json |\n| G3-ring-sampler | CORRECTED: GLM SHIP; integrated/production ring runtime 7/7 | reconcile sampler/integration gates; new-build proof at final acceptance | gates/ring-sampler.md; ring/independent-review-glm.md; runtime/ring-preview-1/ |\n| G4-shaft script / tools | IMPLEMENTED: S1–S6 and tooling leaf checked; tooling GLM SHIP | combined runtime acceptance | gates/shaft-script.md; gates/shaft-tools-progression.md |\n| G4-kinematics / camera | FINAL FOLLOW FIX DELIVERED; recovery inspection tests 152/152 and typecheck PASS | independent re-review of shaft-follow-fix-glm-report.md | gates/shaft-kinematics-camera.md |\n| G5-shaft runtime / finale | FIXED: latest source-level GLM SHIP; corrected desktop dev-2 has five carriers and exact Return restore | dedicated shaft verifier, corrected narrow finale and fresh production proof | gates/shaft-runtime.md; runtime/shaft-smoke/dev-2/ |\n| Dedicated shaft verifier | NOT DELIVERED: producer exhausted HTTP429 retries | resume shaft-verifier-spec.md; shared lifecycle verifier is a different existing script | shaft-verifier-spec.md; shaft-verifier-sol.log |\n| G2–G6 overall acceptance | OPEN; implemented leaves are not final acceptance | remaining mechanical, asset, production/browser, opening and provider-diverse reviews; owner visual acceptance separate | root GATES.md; leaf gates |\n\n## October 6 continuation ownership\n\nThe owner requested reading the recovered handoff and beginning work after clarifying unresolved decisions. Existing overall and leaf gates remain authoritative; no recovery work is discarded.\n\n| Continuation leaf | State | Owned paths | Acceptance |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Shaft browser verifier | IN-FLIGHT | scripts/verify-shaft-inspection.mjs; runtime/shaft/; gates/shaft-runtime-browser.md | shaft-verifier-spec.md S1-S8, two agreeing runs, independent review and parent rerun |\n| Final follow correction review | VERIFIED SOURCE REVIEW | shaft-follow-independent-review-2026-10-06.md only | SHIP; focused shaft 102/102 and typecheck PASS; final browser proof remains separate |\n| Asset and camera acceptance | GLM SOURCE COMPLETE; native footer correction IN-FLIGHT | src/scene/inspection/shaft/camera.ts and camera.test.ts; assets/acceptance-2026-10-06/; camera/blockout-2026-10-06/; camera/footer-fix-2026-10-06/; gates/core-assets.md; gates/camera.md | mobile collision fixed with parent10/10; C4 recorded, D4/C2 open; fresh native worker corrects desktop-material and narrow-final footer observations using measured geometry |\n| Static shaft visual fallback | VERIFIED STATIC LEAF; final overall review pending | src/components/StaticShaftStory.tsx; RingInspection.tsx StaticShaft wrapper only; ShaftStoryLayer.css static selectors; public/inspection/shaft/; static-shaft-2026-10-06/; gates/static-shaft.md | 16 real raster variants; parent production static4/4 PASS; poster zero CAD/tool, reduced inspection zero manufacturing/tool; whole-narrative reduced-motion V4 decision remains pending |\n| Poster metadata availability | VERIFIED SOURCE AND POSTER BROWSER | src/scene/inspection/story.ts; story.test.ts; src/state/inspectionStore.test.ts; poster-metadata-fix-2026-10-06.md | lightweight metadata with no canvas/factory registration; parent source31/31 and production static4/4 PASS, including cold poster zeroCAD/focus |\n| Verifier independent review corrections | IN-FLIGHT, native code-only worker | scripts/verify-shaft-inspection.mjs; runtime/shaft/review-corrections-2026-10-06/ | six source-backed FIX-FIRST items; static GPU leaf complete; paired shaft production runs await corrected verifier readiness |\n| Reduced-motion product decision | WAITING FOR OWNER | no source ownership assigned yet | static poster throughout versus existing static 3D narrative; dependent work waits for explicit answer |\n| Integration and final review | WAITING | parent owns shared-source assignments, PLAN.md, root GATES.md, review-ledger.md and continuation records | rebuild/restart preview, affected checks, production/runtime/opening proof; owner visual acceptance separate |\n\nNative OpenAI seats review the prior GLM follow correction and produce the substantial verifier; proxy-routed GLM review is planned for new OpenAI deliverables. Requested routing is recorded separately from observed serving attribution. No push/deploy is authorized. A checkpoint commit requires a verified manufacturing-owned set and preservation of the unrelated index.\n\n## Status Log\n\n- 2026-10-06 production continuation: final static source/build checks passed (444 tests, production build, static 4/4 and independent core-export acceptance); D4 is checked and C4 recorded. Camera/footer projections pass 8/8, but C2 awaits rendered production shaft proof. Initial shaft production run is preserved after a harness wait for a continuously orbiting narrative camera failed. Atomic entry capture is independently approved. The corrected run exposes actual depth gains before axial stock contact; parent numerical reproduction and fresh native review agree. A separate verifier program-cache instrumentation defect is also confirmed. camera_footer_fix owns kinematics.ts/tests contact-linked progression; verifier_corrections owns harness corrections. No tolerance waiver. GLM native review dispatch failed encrypted-task delivery twice; native substitution is disclosed in shaft-verifier-second-review-2026-10-06.md. Final provider-diverse review remains due. V4 owner choice remains pending.\n\n- 2026-10-06 continuation after rate limits: all three native OpenAI seats failed HTTP429 with partial deliverables preserved. Independent follow review had already completed SHIP with 102/102 focused tests. Asset audits/24 anchor captures completed but their final gate reconciliation is unfinished; mobile card overlap is confirmed by actual decoded vertex membership. Dedicated shaft verifier exists and has a first-run report; remaining harness repairs, causal S2 checks, disposal/restore findings and two complete current runs remain due. Static fallback source exists; clean public raster assets are still missing. Reroute remaining implementation to explicitly requested Z.ai GLM-5.3/high; parent OpenAI reruns and different-provider review remain separate. Servers ended with interrupted sessions; restart them hidden before browser work.\n\n- 2026-10-06 continuation: read recovered handoff, canonical queue/map, measured rig spec, accepted plan and owner storyline, existing gates and final reports. Proxy health is live. Neither :5199 nor :4173 is serving. Asked the explicit V4 reduced-motion product question; independent leaves proceed while the answer is pending.\n\n- 2026-10-06 documentation recovery: reconciled the current state table and review-ledger acceptance summary with the latest saved implementation and reports. Typecheck and 15 inspection/state test files (152 tests) passed during recovery. Historical log entries below are preserved in chronological order; their earlier in-flight/blocked descriptions are not current worker status. See continuation-handoff-2026-10-06.md for the safe resume order and separate backup.\n\n- 2026-10-05: Read continuation, canonical approved plan, owner storyline, asset baseline and repo session-start documents. Prior staged and unstaged changes are extensive; retain them. Graph generation 2026-09-30 is stale for inspection work; live-source fallback required.\n- 2026-10-05: Dispatched native inherited OpenAI workers Hooke (assets), Kant (camera), Bohr (contract). Model/effort request recorded as inherited/high; observed served-model attribution remains to verify from runtime receipts or proxy logs. No different model was silently substituted.\n- 2026-10-05: Bohr failed with retry-limit HTTP 429 before a deliverable. Re-routed the same contract scope to Schrodinger, requested anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 high; parent OpenAI review will provide a different-provider check. Assets and camera remain in flight.\n- 2026-10-05: Parent TypeScript and 5-file/13-test focused inspection baseline passed. Hidden Vite PID 184340 serves localhost:5199. Focused ring runtime baseline dispatched to baseline-ring/.\n- 2026-10-05: Asset measurements returned: approved hashes match, legacy occurrence matches extract, shift is already in exports; four planets and retaining-ring crossings require depth/fit classification. G0 remains open. Sonnet independent mechanical classifier dispatched.\n- 2026-10-05: Native camera worker failed HTTP429 after creating blockout.py; explicitly rerouted completion to Sonnet. Contract delivered by Sonnet and parent OpenAI approved interface freeze with contract-review.md clarifications.\n- 2026-10-05: Ring producer delivered contact/clearance/speed edits. Parent FIX-FIRST: 0.11rad/s forms a full axial band after only12.6deg contact sweep; coverage must be physically sufficient or represented as explicitly compressed high-speed work. Correction requested; lifecycle8turn endpoint test must not simply be weakened.\n- 2026-10-05: All four follow-up Sonnet requests exhausted HTTP429 retries. Their partial files are preserved. Fresh inherited OpenAI workers now own shell, ring correction, mechanical classification and camera/tool compatibility. Previous failed seats closed. Different-provider review remains mandatory and is not inferred from unavailable reviewers.\n- 2026-10-05 (resume): Pasteur, Lorentz, Aristotle, Gibbs, Leibniz and Nash all ended with HTTP429 retry exhaustion. Partial files preserved. Parent (now claude-opus-5-5) takes over Leibniz's integration ownership. Producer routing moves to `codex exec -m zai/glm-5.3` (unique proxy conversations); parent Anthropic review plus GLM read-only reviews provide provider diversity against OpenAI producers.\n- 2026-10-05: Full suite found renderLease light-restore defect: lights were recorded twice (light record, then hidden map after being hidden), so restore re-hid every scene light. Parent fix: early return after light record (renderLease.ts visit). renderLease tests 6/6.\n- 2026-10-05: Housing 3.687 mm finding resolved as classification artifact (mechanical-review/housing-resolution.md): single 2-of-3 parity sample at r 6.01 mm inside a 19.27 mm housing bore, zero triangle crossings, open-shell housing.\n- 2026-10-05: GLM ring sampler review SHIP (ring/independent-review-glm.md); integration/browser not certified by it. Existing verify-ring-inspection.mjs 7/7 cases PASS on integrated lifecycle at :5199 (runtime/ring-integrated-1/report.json).\n- 2026-10-05: Dispatched GLM producers: clearance v3 (camera/clearance-v3-spec.md) and lifecycle verifier (runtime/lifecycle-verifier-spec.md); GLM read-only shell review.\n- 2026-10-05: Z.ai GLM hit its 5-hour usage cap mid-run (clearance, lifecycle, shaft-script producers stopped); lite-assets producer finished first (both tiers published, D1-D3). DeepSeek route then also returned HTTP429 on both producers. Parent continues as sole working seat; DeepSeek read-only review route still worked once (shaft-script SHIP).\n- 2026-10-05: Parent review of clearance-v3: invalid (cutter polar profile collapsed to radius 0 -> TOOL_SAG/e_tool 2.749 mm; hob fed from journal side; contact pairs passed on that bogus tolerance). Superseded by parent-authored scripts/manufacturing/tool_clearance_meridian.py (clearance-v4): exact meridian-profile method for revolution features, exact shaper rectangle, densely sampled tilted hob, explicit e_total.\n- 2026-10-05: Parent completed shaft-script leaf (gates/shaft-script.md S1-S6 checked), added window.__threeRenderer probe (SceneCanvas onCreated), D4 parent export check (legacy housing witness missing: G2 follow-up). Production build PASS; B1/B2 and station2 PASS; verify-ring-inspection 7/7 on fresh :4173 preview (runtime/ring-preview-1).\n- 2026-10-05: Tailwind v4 scans the repo, so producer evidence writes trigger stylesheet rebuilds on the :5199 dev server; runtime verification uses the :4173 production preview.\n- 2026-10-05: clearance-v4 (parent-authored meridian method) CERTIFIED 24/24, deterministic over two runs. DeepSeek review FIX-FIRST (groove-lip relabel, transition contact, e_cad, lead angle) -> fixes -> DeepSeek re-review SHIP with residual items: lead-angle formula (sin g = m_n/(2R) vs implemented asin(m/(2(R-0.708)))), ~31 um land overlap below the measured ramp end waived under generation contact, and latent vacuous-PASS on empty masks in meridian_clearance/rect_clearance. These stay open on gates/camera.md before G0 acceptance. C2 (camera blockout at desktop/390x844) and C4 (budgets/commands) remain open.\n- 2026-10-05: Dispatched producers: shaft tools + progression (DeepSeek, shaft-tools-progression-spec.md) and shaft kinematics + camera (GLM, shaft-kinematics-camera-spec.md). Neither is reviewed or integrated.\n- 2026-10-05 (owner routing update): try openrouter/~google-gemini-flash-latest first; GLM has fresh quota; fall back to gpt-6.1-sol on any trouble. GLM kinematics/camera leaf finished: 5 files / 63 tests, typecheck clean (parent rerun). clearance-v4 empty-mask asserts added, CERTIFIED 24/24, report identical except timestamp; re-review residuals answered in clearance-v4/README.md.\n- 2026-10-05 22:45: Gemini Flash given three seats (tools/progression completion, lifecycle verifier completion, kinematics/camera review). All three ended at 22:53 with OpenRouter HTTP 402 (key can afford 7687 of the 65536 requested output tokens); about 900k tokens used, no final reports, no gate files. Partial edits (cutterOutline.json regenerated, tools.test.ts) leave 63/63 tests passing. No billing/config change. Seats moved to gpt-6.1-sol per owner instruction, plus the shaft runtime leaf (shaft-runtime-spec.md). GLM producing the legacy housing export (assets/legacy-housing-spec.md).\n- 2026-10-06: Results. GLM legacy housing: bundles now 8 nodes (approvedhousing + legacyhousing), registration proof +2.75 mm seat only, deterministic, Default.glb unchanged (D5). Sol tools/progression complete; GLM review SHIP (Sol's own OpenAI reviewer did not count). Sol shaft runtime (90 tests) -> GLM review FIX-FIRST (shaper 0.6 mm offset, previous depth unpopulated, hob thread dispose) -> Sol fixes (98 tests) -> GLM re-review in flight. Sol review of GLM kinematics/camera FIX-FIRST (C1 start, materials camera settle, final card overlap) -> GLM fixes -> Sol re-review: three resolved, new follow-integral regression (kinematics.ts:317) -> GLM fix in flight. Sol lifecycle verifier 12/14 twice; GLM review SHIP; V4 reduced-motion narrative CAD fetch held for owner decision (App.tsx:37).\n- 2026-10-06: Parent integration: shaft story registered (InspectionScene), rig lookup through the hero subtree (fixes finale carriers), static DOM shaft study (store throw removed, test updated), \"Inspect the input shaft\" trigger, ShaftStoryLayer mounted in the dialog (column layout, narrow under header), beat labels in status. Dev smoke (runtime/shaft-smoke/dev-1, dev-2): ready in about 2.2-2.8 s, all beats render, supports delta 2.750 mm, finale assembled from 40 s, Return restores focus with pose error 0. Sol shaft verifier dispatched (shaft-verifier-spec.md).\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content project/work/evidence/JG-035-opening-drafting-table/manufacturing-implementation-2026-10-05/review-ledger.md | Select-Object -Last 120'","aggregated_output":"# Execution review ledger\r\n\r\nThis ledger separates requests, routing attribution, technical verification and owner visual acceptance. Historical planning verdicts do not certify implementation.\r\n\r\n## Requests And Results\r\n\r\n- Native inherited OpenAI G0 source measurement completed. Six approved hashes match. Parent independently reran `measure_g0.py` into `geometry/parent-rerun/`: exit 0 and measurement-summary.json is byte-equivalent as parsed deterministic JSON to the producer's summary. Protected Default.glb SHA-256 remains baseline. Actual observed model per leaf is not established by requested flags.\r\n- Sonnet lifecycle contract completed, requested anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5 high. Parent OpenAI reviewed the actual contract/live source: SHIP for interface freeze with `contract-review.md` clarifications. G1 runtime remains open.\r\n- Sonnet first ring sampler delivered a 0.11 rad/s forming rate. Parent OpenAI: FIX-FIRST due to incomplete circumferential forming while a full axial relief band is shown. Requested correction requires measured per-slice contact coverage and no per-frame sampler allocation. Whole-turn lifecycle assertion must not be weakened just to permit the incorrect rate.\r\n- Native camera worker and subsequent Sonnet follow-up requests exhausted HTTP429 retries. Partial camera/clearance/classification files are preserved. Failed reviewer requests are not SHIP. Fresh inherited workers own shell, ring correction, mechanical classification, camera/tool compatibility and core asset preparation.\r\n- Advisory architecture review launched through `ocx claude --agent fable-advisor`, explicitly requesting claude-fable-5-1 high with only Read/Grep/Glob. Verdict and model evidence are recorded after completion; availability is not assumed.\r\n- That CLI Fable call failed HTTP405 before inference (0 input/output tokens, API error, no verdict); it is unavailable, not SHIP. Explicitly rerouted architecture review to fresh native agent requesting openrouter/~anthropic-claude-opus-latest high. Cost/routing substitution is visible; no provider availability or actual backend identity is inferred from the request alone.\r\n- OpenRouter Opus also returned no verdict: HTTP402 provider credit/output-reservation limit (65536 requested output tokens exceeded the current key allowance). No billing/config limit was changed. Closed the failed seat and inspected the existing model catalog for another different-provider review route.\r\n- Live `ocx models list` includes zai/glm-5.3. Architecture-advisor role explicitly rerouted to a read-only `codex exec -m zai/glm-5.3` high request, producing architecture-advisor-glm.md if successful. This is a Z.ai advisor substitution, not a claim that the Fable model served the review.\r\n- GLM architecture review completed (CLI session 01a10d47-205f-7e42-a851-6b37919d53b0): SHIP lifecycle interface freeze, FIX-FIRST for G1 runtime until planned integration gaps are fixed. Report: architecture-advisor-glm.md. W2 received all five source-backed findings.\r\n- Per-request attribution for that unique GLM conversation 12a1d5e2b17f0e4fe3bb406bb68a040b: ocx-762efa011f9e0d1c880fad93f0d573b8, ocx-ce54a4a3250ae0fdebc508c432f302d0, ocx-b25307af18d492faa82fd5d75b671407; requested zai/glm-5.3, resolved/served glm-5.3, provider zai, requested effort high, HTTP200. This is proxy-side observed served-model accounting, not independently verified backend effort. The provider differs from the adopting/integration OpenAI producer.\r\n\r\n## Attribution Limits\r\n\r\n- Gemini Flash trial (openrouter/~google-gemini-flash-latest via codex exec): route probe OK; three seats each failed with HTTP 402 credit/max_tokens after 4-8 minutes; no deliverable or verdict. Not counted as review.\r\n- Sol (gpt-6.1-sol via codex exec, OpenAI provider): route probe OK; producers for tools/progression completion, lifecycle verifier, shaft runtime; read-only reviewer for the GLM kinematics/camera leaf (different provider from producer).\r\n\r\n- Resume: GLM ring sampler review (ring/independent-review-glm.md) SHIP for sampler math, coverage, ordering, allocation-free sampling and high-speed scaling; vitest blocked in its read-only sandbox, so it re-executed timeline.ts via Node. Notes: README test-count prose stale; recorded InspectionScene hash predates integration drift.\r\n- All six native workers ended HTTP429. Parent model is now claude-opus-5-5 (Anthropic). Parent reviews are Anthropic-provider; GLM reviews are Z.ai-provider; OpenAI-produced leaves therefore receive two other-provider checks where both run.\r\n\r\nProxy usage records currently associate multiple native agents with one shared conversation scope. OpenAI rows report requested/resolved/served gpt-6.1-sol and HTTP200; Anthropic rows report requested/resolved Sonnet and HTTP200 without upstream servedModel. Per-seat association is not uniquely proven from that scope. No producer/reviewer completion is claimed from these aggregate records alone.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance\r\n\r\nUpdated 2026-10-06 from the final leaf evidence and [recovered handoff](continuation-handoff-2026-10-06.md): implementation is present; overall G0–G6 acceptance remains open. Earlier request entries above are historical, not current worker status.\r\n\r\n- G0: source measurements, neighbour classification and deterministic clearance-v4 CERTIFIED 24/24 are recorded. Remaining mechanical review, camera blockout C2 and budgets/commands C4 still prevent overall G0 closure. Invalid clearance-v3 is superseded.\r\n- G1: shared shell has GLM SHIP and parent reruns; ring/shaft integration and static/dialog layers exist. The lifecycle verifier has GLM SHIP but actual runtime is 12/14 twice: reduced-motion narrative CAD loading leaves V4 open, with V6 parent rerun due. Verifier acceptance does not establish app behavior acceptance.\r\n- G2/G3: full/lite eight-node study bundles include legacy housing; independent export acceptance D4 remains open. Corrected ring sampler has GLM SHIP and integrated/production runtime 7/7. Reconcile stale leaf checkboxes against that evidence; do not treat the original forming-coverage finding as still uncorrected.\r\n- G4/G5: shaft script/tool progression and runtime are implemented. Tooling review is GLM SHIP. Runtime fixes received source-level GLM SHIP in [shaft-runtime-rereview-glm.md](shaft-runtime-rereview-glm.md); that reviewer could not run Vitest/typecheck. The final analytic follow correction in [shaft-follow-fix-glm-report.md](shaft-follow-fix-glm-report.md) still needs independent re-review after the earlier Sol finding.\r\n- Recovery independently reran typecheck and 15 inspection/state test files: 152/152 PASS. These checks do not replace runtime visibility/performance proof.\r\n- Corrected desktop development smoke has five carriers, assembled finale, 2.750 mm support delta and Return pose error 0. Corrected narrow finale and final production shaft evidence are still missing. The dedicated shaft verifier producer exhausted HTTP429 retries without a deliverable; its spec is the restart point.\r\n\r\nG6, final provider-diverse integration review and owner runtime visual acceptance remain open. No commit, push or deployment was performed during recovery or this documentation/graph follow-up.\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
